  "evidence": "SwissWatchExpo 49534 original specimen. All 12 original gallery images inspected 17 November 2026; movement 8 reviewed at 1200px from original 2034x2035 file. Visible 3135 bridge stamp and numeric 31 rotor inscription. Case engraving 7 reads 16613 T, exact base 16613 attributed by listing; no new T alias. Blue dial and bezel insert, two-tone Oyster/flip-lock visible. Dealer attributes 2007–2008, 40mm steel/18k yellow-gold components and sapphire crystal; these remain attributions, not material assay or independent chronology. Dealer notes bezel-insert crack/scratches; specimen condition is not a required reference trait. No transfer to black-dial or later ceramic specimens. No transfer to neighbouring references or other unopened specimens; original fitment, service status, full chronology and user-watch authenticity are not independently established. Existing photographs remain separate specimens. Overall execution/period research remains incomplete.",
